 "issue": 1795,
 "issue_title": "Bug: reject empty columns in ArFrame.from_records",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n`ArFrame.from_records()` silently drops all rows when dict records are passed with `columns=[]`.\n\n## Why it matters\n`from_records()` is a public constructor. Passing an explicit empty `columns` list should either be rejected clearly or preserve the requested row count as an empty-column frame. Returning `(0, 0)` from non-empty input silently loses data and can hide caller mistakes.\n\n## Evidence\n- `arnio/frame.py::ArFrame.from_records()` accepts `columns` as a list/tuple of strings but does not reject an empty list for dict records.\n- It delegates to `pandas.DataFrame.from_records(records, columns=columns)` and then `from_pandas()`.\n- With non-empty dict records and `columns=[]`, pandas returns an empty `(0, 0)` frame, so Arnio loses the source row count.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n```python\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.ArFrame.from_records([{\"a\": 1}, {\"a\": 2}], columns=[])\nprint(frame.shape)\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\nEither:\n\n- reject `columns=[]` with a clear `ValueError`, or\n- return an empty-column frame that still preserves the two source rows, if Arnio wants to support that shape.\n\n## Actual behavior\nThe constructor returns an empty frame with no rows:\n\n```text\n(0, 0)\n```\n\n## Suggested direction\nReject empty `columns` for dict records unless empty-column frames with preserved row counts are fully supported here. Add tests for dict records with `columns=[]` and for normal explicit column subsets.\n\n## References\n- `arnio/frame.py::ArFrame.from_records`\n- `tests/test_frame.py`\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1795",
 "pr": 2125,
 "pr_title": "fix: raise ValueError for empty columns in ArFrame.from_records with \u2026",
 "pr_body": "Fixes #1795\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n\r\n`ArFrame.from_records()` silently returned an empty `(0, 0)` frame when dict records were passed with `columns=[]`. This caused silent data loss with no indication to the caller.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n**`arnio/frame.py`**\r\n- Added a `ValueError` guard in the dict branch of `ArFrame.from_records()` that rejects `columns=[]` with a clear, actionable message pointing the caller to use `columns=None` instead.\r\n\r\n**`tests/test_frame.py`**\r\n- `test_from_records_dict_empty_columns_raises` \u2014> verifies `columns=[]` raises `ValueError`\r\n- `test_from_records_dict_empty_columns_message_is_helpful` \u2014> verifies the error message mentions `columns=None`\r\n- `test_from_records_dict_columns_none_infers_from_keys` \u2014> verifies default behavior (infer from keys) is unchanged\r\n- `test_from_records_dict_explicit_valid_columns_subset` \u2014> verifies a valid non-empty explicit column list still works correctly\r\n\r\n## Behavior\r\n\r\n**Before**\r\n```python\r\nframe = ar.ArFrame.from_records([{\"a\": 1}, {\"a\": 2}], columns=[])\r\nprint(frame.shape)  # (0, 0) \u2014 silent data loss\r\n```\r\n\r\n**After**\r\n```python\r\nframe = ar.ArFrame.from_records([{\"a\": 1}, {\"a\": 2}], columns=[])\r\n# ValueError: columns must not be empty when records are dicts;\r\n# pass columns=None to infer column names from the record keys\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- Scoped strictly to the dict records path in `from_records()` as requested\r\n- Existing behavior for `columns=None` and valid explicit column subsets is fully preserved\r\n- 8 pre-existing test failures in `test_describe_*` are unrelated to this change and were present on `main` before this branch",
 "fix_commit": "b64e3354789043ab8949947d9f823851c0669c46",
